{"id":"viarhona","title":"ViaRhôna: Lake Geneva to the Mediterranean","who":"EuroVelo 17 · classic cycle route","when":"Best April–October","vehicle":"Bicycle, 10–14 days","kind":"bike","color":"#0284c7","summary":"About 800 km down the Rhône from Lake Geneva to the sea, mostly on greenways and quiet roads: Alpine lakes, Lyon, Côtes-du-Rhône vineyards, Roman Orange, the Pont d'Avignon, Arles and the Camargue, ending at Sète. Mostly flat or downhill with the mistral at your back.","sources":[{"label":"ViaRhôna official site","url":"https://en.viarhona.com/the-route/a-truly-european-cycle-route"},{"label":"France Vélo Tourisme: ViaRhôna","url":"https://en.francevelotourisme.com/itineraire/viarhona"},{"label":"Freewheeling France: the ViaRhôna","url":"https://freewheelingfrance.com/bike-routes-in-france/via-rhona-bike-route.html"}],"approximate":"Main towns on the route; the path follows cycleways only approximately.","km":679,"bbox":[3.6958,43.4014,6.8016,46.4074],"stops":[{"name":"Saint-Gingolph","place":"Saint-Gingolph, France","at":[46.389,6.7757],"text":"Official start on Lake Geneva's French shore.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Saint-Gingolph_depuis_Le_Grammont.jpg/500px-Saint-Gingolph_depuis_Le_Grammont.jpg","page":"Saint-Gingolph","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint-Gingolph_depuis_Le_Grammont.jpg","credit":"Christian David","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Thonon","place":"Thonon-les-Bains, France","at":[46.3731,6.4779],"text":"Along the lake.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/200505-Thonon_Hotel_de_Ville.JPG/500px-200505-Thonon_Hotel_de_Ville.JPG","page":"Thonon-les-Bains","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:200505-Thonon_Hotel_de_Ville.JPG","credit":"Semnoz","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Geneva","place":"Genève, Switzerland","at":[46.2018,6.1466],"text":"Where the Rhône leaves the lake.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org